      "visit_number": 10
    },
    {
      "sequence": 116,
      "operation_number": 36,
      "type": "visit_note_recorded",
      "visit_number": 10,
      "text": "Beneath the oath-mirrors, Maelith owned the public effect of the equinox slight and Vaudren accepted without demanding a false confession of motive. The personal bond, guarantor shares, reserve pledge, and associated instruments acquired witnesses. Caelir then offered every house a true partial victory that required it to leave the others."
    },
    {
      "sequence": 117,
      "operation_number": 37,
      "type": "encounter_consequence_recorded",
      "encounter_id": "the-white-hart-gallery",
      "text": "Maelith publicly declares for reciprocal personal surety and preserved royal custody. Mara Venn is named expressly as neither hostage, ward, nor surety."
    },
    {
      "sequence": 118,
      "operation_number": 38,
      "type": "encounter_consequence_recorded",
      "encounter_id": "the-red-rose-pavilion",
      "text": "Vaudren publicly declares after Maelith owns the public diminution. The Rose accepts neutral authorship and the proclamation office without winning a general ruling on precedence."
    },
    {
      "sequence": 119,
      "operation_number": 39,
      "type": "encounter_consequence_recorded",
      "encounter_id": "the-twilight-laurel-apartments",
      "text": "House Eiral withholds the Twilight Laurel from the narrow seven-seasonal-banner coalition. Theron separately confirms that the Chamberlain’s official certification duty has not moved with the house."
    },
    {
      "sequence": 120,
      "operation_number": 40,
      "type": "encounter_consequence_recorded",
      "encounter_id": "the-unfurling-branch",
      "text": "Ilyrion supports the rescue and withholds declaration because protection against redirection is not equal co-custody. Saelira refuses to let departure be counted as assent to the status bargain."
    },
    {
      "sequence": 121,
      "operation_number": 41,
      "type": "encounter_visited",
      "visit_number": 11,
      "encounter_id": "the-amber-quill-archive",
      "party_label": ""
    },
    {
      "sequence": 122,
      "operation_number": 41,
      "type": "clue_spotted",
      "clue_id": "certification-and-support-are-separate-acts",
      "visit_number": 11
    },
    {
      "sequence": 123,
      "operation_number": 41,
      "type": "visit_note_recorded",
      "visit_number": 11,
      "text": "After the Masque, Pelion separated the Crown petition from the surety bond, public credit, reserve and ward contracts, liability schedule, audit, and Orison’s civil-refusal instrument. Ilyrion’s unsigned recognition compact remained a possible later act and was not allowed to masquerade as a present concession."
    },
    {
      "sequence": 124,
      "operation_number": 42,
      "type": "encounter_consequence_recorded",
      "encounter_id": "the-amber-quill-archive",
      "text": "Namaris declares on the finished architecture: exact definitions, adverse authority, indexed associated instruments, and a correction procedure showing which seals depend on each article."
    },
    {
