      "visit_number": 12
    },
    {
      "sequence": 133,
      "operation_number": 43,
      "type": "visit_note_recorded",
      "visit_number": 12,
      "text": "Seven banners provisionally sealed the first complete text. The royal advocate found a collision between Serathiel’s command and Naevra’s power to stop anything threatening the “safe execution” of the undertaking. Theron ruled the phrase material and released Maelith, Serathiel, Vaudren, and Serevin."
    },
    {
      "sequence": 134,
      "operation_number": 44,
      "type": "encounter_consequence_recorded",
      "encounter_id": "the-chamber-of-the-fourfold-petition",
      "text": "The phrase “safe execution of the undertaking” is struck. Naevra may stop a defined risk of damage to the Sunseed or a use beyond the undertaking; she may not command route, tactics, Orison’s government, or ordinary expedition safety."
    },
    {
      "sequence": 135,
      "operation_number": 45,
      "type": "encounter_consequence_recorded",
      "encounter_id": "the-red-rose-pavilion",
      "text": "The journal initially records that Vaudren’s seal remains attached because the public-credit article did not change."
    },
    {
      "sequence": 136,
      "operation_number": 46,
      "type": "operation_voided",
      "target_operation_number": 45,
      "reason": "The journal treated Vaudren’s seal as independent of functional authorship. A broad royal safety veto would have converted the undertaking into a royal act, so Vaudren’s seal released with the other dependent seals."
    },
    {
      "sequence": 137,
      "operation_number": 47,
      "type": "encounter_consequence_recorded",
      "encounter_id": "the-red-rose-pavilion",
      "text": "Vaudren’s seal is released by the broad royal safety veto: neutral authorship would have become a title over a functionally royal act. The Rose will reaffirm only after authority and the shared title are exact."
    },
    {
      "sequence": 138,
      "operation_number": 48,
      "type": "encounter_consequence_recorded",
      "encounter_id": "the-chamber-of-the-fourfold-petition",
      "text": "Maelith and Serevin reaffirm the corrected authority article. Serathiel waits for the eight-day campaign schedule; Vaudren waits for the shared title. Orelle, Namaris, and Thalan remain sealed."
    },
    {
      "sequence": 139,
      "operation_number": 49,
      "type": "encounter_visited",
      "visit_number": 13,
      "encounter_id": "the-hall-of-first-frost",
      "party_label": ""
    },
    {
      "sequence": 140,
      "operation_number": 49,
      "type": "clue_spotted",
      "clue_id": "necessity-does-not-waive-seasonal-balance",
      "visit_number": 13
    },
    {
      "sequence": 141,
      "operation_number": 49,
      "type": "visit_note_recorded",
      "visit_number": 13,
      "text": "On Conclave morning, Thalan reviewed the corrected veto, eight-day term, sunset, and shared title. Tamsin agreed to accept royal joinder after certification, never as the price of certification, and only within powers the seven-banner text already allowed."
    },
    {
      "sequence": 142,
      "operation_number": 50,
      "type": "encounter_consequence_recorded",
      "encounter_id": "the-hall-of-first-frost",
      "text": "Thalan keeps its seal and will present the narrow necessity finding. Voluntary royal joinder may strengthen the undertaking, but it cannot be allowed to supply validity the seven banners already possess."
    },
    {
      "sequence": 143,
      "operation_number": 51,
